+## Execution Order
+
+**Wave 1** fires first with all 12 independent tasks in parallel: T01 (config schema), T02 (prompt-utils library), T09 (RED-verification adapter contract), T14 (CI workflow), T15 (hygiene contract), T20 (Parallelize OWNS addition), T21 (multi-stage grammar), T24 (Plan spec frontmatter), T29 (reviewer-protocol quick-tier + design checklist), T34 (anchor index files), T40 (u14-lint slug fix), T41 (Replan boundary section). These share no files and have no inter-dependencies. Wave 1 completion gates Wave 2.
+
+**Wave 2** fires after Wave 1 with 9 tasks in parallel: T03 (universal dispatcher, forked from T01+T02 stage), T06 (agent model_role frontmatter), T08 (dual-mode test-writer), T10 (four RED adapter scripts), T16 (Integrate CI gate), T25 (Structure UI affordances), T26 (Parallelize reference-gate wave termination), T31 (Plan post-approval split orchestration), T38 (commit-hygiene invariants). No internal file overlaps. Wave 2 completion gates Wave 3.
+
+**Wave 3** fires after Wave 2 with 4 tasks in parallel: T04 (codex-shim retirement), T05 (Implement routing chain + telemetry, forked from T01+T03 stage), T33 (G4 cache-probe script + spike report), T35 (anchor-refresh script + structure Section-Anchor spec). T05 touches `skills/implement/SKILL.md`; no other Wave 3 task does. T35 touches `skills/structure/SKILL.md`; T25 (Wave 2) also touched it but different waves do not conflict. Wave 3 completion gates Wave 4.
+
+**Wave 4** fires after Wave 3 with 1 task: T11 (Implement-skill RED-verification gate + implementer split-mode awareness, forked from T08+T10 stage). T11 must be isolated in its own wave because it edits `skills/implement/SKILL.md` (also edited by T05 in Wave 3 and T27 in Wave 5) and `agents/qrspi-implementer.md` (also edited by T15 in Wave 1, different wave). Wave 4 completion gates Wave 5.
+
+**Wave 5** fires after Wave 4 with 2 tasks in parallel: T12 (Plan dispatch-order note, single-parent chain from T11) and T27 (Implement reference-gate pause + VFR dispatch, multi-parent from T24+T26). T12 edits `skills/plan/SKILL.md`; T27 edits `skills/implement/SKILL.md` — no overlap. Both Wave 5 tasks have disjoint file sets. Wave 5 completion gates Wave 6.
+
+**Wave 6** fires after Wave 5 with 2 tasks in parallel: T13 (shared BATS helper + Slice 2 pins, multi-parent from T08+T11+T12 stage) and T28 (visual-fidelity reviewer refinement, multi-parent from T24+T27 stage). No file overlap between T13 and T28. Wave 6 is the critical convergence point — T13's output gates the majority of Wave 7. Wave 6 completion gates Wave 7.
+
+**Wave 7** fires after Wave 6 with 10 tasks in parallel: T17, T18, T19 (three Slice 3 BATS pins), T22 (helper migration), T23 (Slice 4 pins), T30 (Slice 5 pins), T32 (plan post-approval split pin), T37 (no-summary-shim pin), T39 (worktree-exclude append + commit-hygiene pin), T42 (replan boundary pin). All 10 tasks have disjoint file sets — each creates new test files or touches distinct skill/agent files. T39 edits `skills/implement/SKILL.md`, which was last touched by T27 in Wave 5; no other Wave 7 task touches it. Wave 7 is the largest parallel fan-out in the plan. Wave 7 completion gates Wave 8.
+
+**Wave 8** fires after Wave 7 with 2 tasks in parallel: T07 (Slice 1 unit pins, multi-parent from T03+T05+T06 stage) and T36 (Slice 7 G4 pins, multi-parent from T13+T33+T34+T35 stage). Both create new BATS test files with no overlaps. Wave 8 completion gates Wave 9.
+
+**Wave 9** fires last with 1 conditional task: T43 (G4 Path B cache_control activation). T43 is a NO-OP if the T33 spike report records Path A; the Implement orchestrator evaluates the precondition before dispatch. T43 edits `docs/qrspi/2026-05-17-v07-release/config.md`, which no other task touches.
+
+Waves that can fire concurrently at the same logical level are listed within each wave above. No wave-to-wave skipping is permitted — each wave depends on the prior wave's merge commit (or stage commit) to be complete.
