+## Worktree-aware setup validation
+
+This is a pure script-and-markdown project — there are no JavaScript/TypeScript build artifacts, no `node_modules`, no compiled output, and no framework-specific build directories. No `.worktrees/**` path exclusions are needed in `.gitignore` or CI configuration. Per-task worktrees created by Implement will hold only shell scripts, markdown files, BATS test files, and JSON artifacts; none of these produce derivative build output that would need to be excluded from other worktrees' views of the repository. The worktree-local `.git/info/exclude` append for `.qrspi-commit-msg.txt` (authored by task-39) is the only per-worktree filesystem advisory needed for this release.
